imore, MD 21234\r\nOffice: 410-444-3800\r\nCell: 443-725-6292\r\nFax: 410-881-4535", "currentorpast": "Past", "servicehelpful": "Yes"}], "houseHoldName": "SUZETTE STURGIS", "caregiverArray": [{"caseid": "3304756", "caregiverid": "1156324", "caregiverage": "29", "caregiverdob": "1990-04-15T04:00:00.000Z", "caregivername": "68452f73-2a6c-4927-b5ea-9b6efd0fc8ef", "caregivernametext": "", "caregiverrelationship": "Self"}], "referralsource": " Please note that the case head is now Evelyn Griffin, not Suzette Sturgis.  Jonia lives in the home with her sister, Ms. Griffin.   \nClient was removed from her mother''s care  (Suzette Sturgis) last year due to neglect and most recently Jonia reports running away due to her mother (Suzette Sturgis) calling her inappropriate names and choking her. Ms. Griffin reports that they don’t have a lot of contact with their mother but has the ability to call her. Client (jonia) most recently had suicide ideation of cutting herself on the writs tang attending Anne Arundel Medical Center. Client (Jonia) reports that her mother’s actions and family triggers her behavior since she doesn’t feel loved all the time. Client is not allowed to have door closed and is monitored by her sister for suicide ideations. Client''s mom (Suzette Sturgis) has history of substance abuse, mental health concerns and last year allowed client to have relationship with a 20 year old man.\n\nClient''s sister would benefit from recourses to help client and her family. It appears that Ms. Griffin is very good at trying to provide Jonia with all that she needs but admitted to needing more help to deal with this situation. \n\nJonia is residing in the home of her sister Ms. Griffin. Ms. Griffin has reports that her children does not need services.  Jonia is enrolled at Phoenix Academy in Annapolis MD, sees a school psychologist and she has an IEP in place. Jonia reports that she would like to continue to reside in the home of Ms. Griffin. \n\n\n\n", "timeCompletion": "Initial", "caseheaddatetime": "1969-12-22", "childdescription": "Jonia reports that she likes her present home and living with her sister, but that her mother, Ms. Sturgis is strict and doesn''t care of her well.  Jonia also reports that she is seeing a therapist at school but is having a hard time building rapport with her because she doesn''t trust her.  Jonia reports that she is doing well in school and is passing all her classes.       ", "caregiverdescription": "Ms. Griffin reports that she is caring for her sister, Jonia since September 2019 due to her mother relapsing on illicit substances. Ms. Griffin reports that Jonia attends school (phoenix academy) and is seeing a school psychologist (Ms. Eokkeeffe). Ms. Griffin reports that Jonia does not like to be disciplined by her mother and does not have a good relationship with her mother. Ms. Griffin reports that she does make Jonia keep her door open at night for safety and that Jonia is not permitted to use an electronic device as she has abused that in the past by posting pictures of herself to older men. Ms. Griffin reports that her mother does not come to the home to  see Jonia often and has no concerns with her.   \n\n\n"}, "supervisorname": "Emilee Howard", "assessmentStaus": "Accepted", "assessmentactor": [{"intakeservicerequestactorid": "fc130c04-c815-4d32-848e-11b3d6a3575b"}, {"intakeservicerequestactorid": null}], "oldsupervisorname": "Emilee Howard", "familyCultureYouth": {"ritual_scale": "0", "sexual_scale": "0", "cultural_scale": "0", "language_scale": "0", "ritual_comments": "Ms. Griffin reports that the family has family dinner''s, Thanksgivings together yearly. ", "ritual_strength": false, "sexual_comments": "No Concerns or observations. ", "cultural_comments": "Ms. Griffin reports that the family practice Christianity and believes in a higher power. Family and caregiver agreed there are no cultural issues that  will impact service delivery, safety and the well being of the family", "cultural_stren